 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the city of Rensselaer, county of Rensselaer to discontinue use of and convey certain parkland",
    "basePrintNo": "S5511",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5511-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Rensselaer County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5511\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize the city of Rensselaer, county of Rensselaer to\ndiscontinue use of\nand convey certain parkland\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill will allow the city of\nRensselaer to exchange a portion of land with Oreste Frank Orciuoli to\nfacilitate access and use of the Coyne Memorial Playground.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS;\nSection 1 authorizes the city of\nRensselaer to alienate a portion of parklands and convey such portion\nto Oreste Frank Orciuoli in exchange for an equal amount of land to be\nused as parklands.\nSection 2 requires the city of Rensselaer to use\nproceeds and/or land received in such exchange for park purposes.\nSection 3 outlines the property to be alienated by the city.\nSection 4 outlines the property to be received in replacement of the\nalienated parkland.\nSection 5 outlines the requirements the city must\nmeet if such parcel being alienated has received funding pursuant to\nthe federal land and water conservation fund.\nSection 6 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe City of Rensselaer and Oreste Frank Orciuoli own\nlands adjacent to one another between Columbia Turnpike and Cambridge\nAvenue. Each would like to exchange a portion of their respective\nlands. Such transaction will facilitate the access and use of the\nCoyne Memorial Playground and provide additional rear property and\nsetback to a commercial building on Columbia Turnpike.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
