    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5511B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn  act  to  authorize the city of Rensselaer, county of Rensselaer to\ndiscontinue use of and convey certain parkland\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill will allow the city of Rensselaer to exchange a  portion  of\nland  with  Oreste  Frank Orciuoli to facilitate access and use of the\nCoyne Memorial Playground\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 authorizes the city of Rensselaer to alienate a  portion  of\npark  lands  and  convey  such  portion  to  Oreste  Frank Orciuoli in\nexchange for an equal amount of land to be used as parklands.  Section\n2 requires the city of Rensselaer to use proceeds and/or land received\nin such exchange for park purposes. Section 3 outlines the property to\nbe  alienated  by  the  city.  Section  4  outlines the property to be\nreceived in replacement of the alienated parkland. Section 5  outlines\nthe requirements the city must meet if such parcel being alienated has\nreceived  funding  pursuant to the federal land and water conservation\nfund. Section 6 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe City of Rensse1aer and Oreste Frank Orciuoli own lands adjacent to\none another between Columbia Turnpike and Cambridge Avenue. Each would\nlike to exchange a portion of their respective lands. Such transaction\nwill facilitate the access and use of the  Coyne  Memorial  Playground\nand  provide  additional  rear  property  and  setback to a commercial\nbuilding on Columbia Turnpike.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
